 ## Overview
-Neural Photon Field Rendering is a GPU-based path tracing method that estimates direct illumination via standard ray-marching techniques and approximates indirect global illumination by querying a pre-trained neural field [S1]. Unlike traditional path tracers that recursively trace secondary rays for global illumination, this method computes only the first volume interaction and uses the neural network to predict the incoming radiance $L_i$ from the rest of the scene [S1].
+Neural Photon Field Rendering is a GPU-based path tracing method that estimates direct illumination via standard ray-marching techniques and approximates indirect global illumination by querying a pre-trained neural field [S1]. Unlike traditional path tracers that recursively trace secondary rays for global illumination, this method computes only the first volume interaction and uses the neural network to predict the incoming radiance $L_i$ from the rest of the scene [S1]. It builds on [Path Tracing with Volume Interaction](3320-path-tracing-with-volume-interaction.md) and differs from [Emissive Volume Rendering](3398-emissive-volume-rendering.md) by explicitly decoupling direct and indirect terms via a learned photon field [S1].
 
